    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="14" relname="background">Intuitiveness is the most fundamental concept regarding a good user interface.</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="14" relname="span">The key point of Intuitiveness is easy to learn, especially for the first-time-user.</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="16" relname="preparation">In most cases, Intuitiveness affects users from the following two situations:</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="17" relname="span">1. Users, including those novices, can figure it out how to operate correctly,</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="4" relname="concession">even though there is only minimal interaction or assistance available from the user documentation.</segment>
        <segment id="6" parent="16" relname="list">2. Users, including those novices, can pick it up quickly and easily whenever there is an unambiguous situation.</segment>
        <segment id="7" parent="13" relname="span">However, Intuitiveness comes from the users' previous personal experience, knowledge, and skills.</segment>
        <segment id="8" parent="18" relname="span">Intuitiveness cannot be inherited from the Heaven directly.</segment>
        <segment id="9" parent="10" relname="condition">If a user has some word processing experience,</segment>
        <segment id="10" parent="20" relname="span">he/she will not have much difficulty to figure out how to use different word processing software, such as Microsofts Word or Corels WordPerfect,</segment>
        <segment id="11" parent="20" relname="concession">even though there is no the user documentation or the tutors assistance available.</segment>
        <group id="12" type="span"/>
        <group id="13" type="span" parent="12" relname="span"/>
        <group id="14" type="span" parent="21" relname="span"/>
        <group id="15" type="span" parent="2" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="16" type="multinuc" parent="15" relname="span"/>
